      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the fraction of the items on the menu that can be eaten, we first need to find the total number of items on the menu. According to the problem, the four meatless dishes represent one fifth of the menu. Let's use \\( x \\) to represent the total number of items on the menu. We can set up the following equation:\n\n\\[ \\frac{4}{x} = \\frac{1}{5} \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( x \\), we can cross-multiply:\n\n\\[ 4 \\times 5 = 1 \\times x \\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[ 20 = x \\]\n\nSo, the total number of items on the menu is 20. Out of these 20 items, 4 are meatless and 3 of those are made with pasta, which contains gluten. Therefore, the number of items we can eat is:\n\n\\[ 4 \\text{ (meatless dishes)} + 0 \\text{ (no gluten pasta)} + 0 \\text{ (grain-based pasta)} - 3 \\text{ (gluten-containing meatless dishes)} = 1 \\]\n\nThe fraction of the items on the menu that can be eaten is:\n\n\\[ \\frac{1}{20} \\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{20}}",
